From 9c629ddfc2a3ce9b8555e3586a80522afda47c98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Manoj Sekar <sekar@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 10:53:50 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: Implement HAL scan functionality

Add nl80211 scan implementation to enable sending scan requests from
prplMesh to the driver and retrieving scan dump results. This completes
the missing HAL scan support for the nl80211 backend and adds stub
implementations for the onewifi (RDK) backend.

Changes in nl80211:

    Subscribe to the nl80211 scan multicast group on socket attach and
expose the socket fd to the event loop; reset on detach.
    Implement netlink event processing in the base class, dispatching
received messages to a new pure virtual handler in derived classes.
    Implement scan trigger, scan dump, cached scan dump, and scan abort
in the monitor HAL using native nl80211 commands.
    Parse BSS scan result attributes (BSSID, frequency, signal strength,
information elements) into the prplMesh scan result structure.
    Handle scan completion and abort kernel events in the monitor HAL,
driving the prplMesh scan state machine accordingly.
    Add no-op override stubs in AP and STA HALs to satisfy the pure
virtual interface.

Signed-off-by: Manoj Sekar <sekar@qti.qualcomm.com>
